WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.027
Step 1. Open the allergy form. From an open encounter of the patient,

1.2
00:00:05.027 --> 00:00:08.211
select the Edit pencil in the Allergies panel.

1.3
00:00:08.211 --> 00:00:11.826
The form shows the patient's saved allergies.

2.1
00:00:11.826 --> 00:00:13.780
Step 2. Find the allergy.

2.2
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:20.006
The Substance column shows the allergen, which you cannot change on a saved allergy.

3.1
00:00:20.006 --> 00:00:22.986
Step 3. Change the clinical status.

3.2
00:00:22.986 --> 00:00:27.976
Open the row menu with the three dots, and select Mark Inactive.

3.3
00:00:27.976 --> 00:00:31.440
In the form, an inactive row is faded.

4.1
00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:37.187
Step 4. Change the verification status. The form labels it Status.

4.2
00:00:37.187 --> 00:00:40.935
Select the new value, such as Presumed.

5.1
00:00:40.935 --> 00:00:44.988
Step 5. Change the criticality, occurrence and note.

5.2
00:00:44.988 --> 00:00:50.900
The form shows a Note field under each saved allergy; type the note there.

6.1
00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:54.677
Step 6. Save the changes. Select Save Changes.

6.2
00:00:54.677 --> 00:01:00.582
Care links every saved allergy in the form to this encounter, changed or not.

6.3
00:01:00.582 --> 00:01:04.226
The Allergies panel shows the new values.
